@meta
id: 23-09
title: Drill — move a whole section
chapter: 23
type: drill
skills: folds
par: 40
minutes: 5
reps: 6
vscode: select from heading to heading by eye, cut, scroll, paste
open: runbook.md
vimrc: let g:markdown_folding=1 | e

@brief
The runbook lists rollback before deploy. Six times: move the whole
`## Rollback` section — heading, body and the blank line after it — so
it comes after `## Deploy` and before `## Verify`.

Markdown heading folds are on: every section is one fold. Never select
by hand.

@keys
| `zc` | close the fold the search just opened |
| `dd` on a closed fold | cut the whole section |
| `p` on a closed fold | paste after the whole section |

@hints
`/## Rollback` then `zc` then `dd` cuts the section as one line.
--
`/## Deploy` then `zc` then `p` drops it after the whole Deploy
section, not after its heading.

@solution
    /## Rollback<Enter> zc dd /## Deploy<Enter> zc p :wq<Enter>

Thirty-five keystrokes to move fourteen lines, and none of them was a
count. This is the fold trick in its purest form: heading folds give
you a section as a unit, and a closed unit moves with `dd` and `p`.
No text object does this.

Vim's markdown filetype builds these folds when `g:markdown_folding`
is set; the dojo set it for this lesson. In your own vimrc it is one
line.

@start runbook.md
# Payments release runbook

Read the whole thing before you start. Every step is reversible until
the migration runs.

## Rollback

1. Scale the payments service to zero.
2. Restore the previous image tag in the deployment.
3. Run `npm run db:migrate:down` once.
4. Scale back up and watch the error rate for ten minutes.

Rollback takes about four minutes end to end.

## Deploy

1. Merge the release branch.
2. Wait for the pipeline to publish the image.
3. Apply the migration with `npm run db:migrate`.
4. Roll the deployment.

## Verify

Check the refund dashboard. Declined payments should stay flat and
refund latency should not move.

@expected runbook.md
# Payments release runbook

Read the whole thing before you start. Every step is reversible until
the migration runs.

## Deploy

1. Merge the release branch.
2. Wait for the pipeline to publish the image.
3. Apply the migration with `npm run db:migrate`.
4. Roll the deployment.

## Rollback

1. Scale the payments service to zero.
2. Restore the previous image tag in the deployment.
3. Run `npm run db:migrate:down` once.
4. Scale back up and watch the error rate for ten minutes.

Rollback takes about four minutes end to end.

## Verify

Check the refund dashboard. Declined payments should stay flat and
refund latency should not move.
